1. Basic Properties
JavaScript
let str = "Hello World";

str.length; // 11 (returns character count)
str[0];      // "H" (gets character by index)

2. Searching & Checking
JavaScript
str.includes("World"); // true (checks if substring exists)
str.indexOf("o");      // 4 (returns first position of 'o')
str.startsWith("H");   // true
str.endsWith("d");     // true

3. Modifying Strings
JavaScript
str.toUpperCase();     // "HELLO WORLD"
str.toLowerCase();     // "hello world"
str.trim();            // Removes whitespace from both ends

4. Cutting & Splitting
JavaScript
str.slice(0, 5);       // "Hello" (cuts from index 0 to 4)
str.replace("World", "JS"); // "Hello JS"
str.split(" ");        // ["Hello", "World"] (turns string into array)
💡 Core Pattern: String Iteration
JavaScript
// Loop through every character in a string
for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
    console.log(str[i]);
}
